    "goal": "Characterize a perfused microfluidic channel: report mean velocity and wall shear stress at the given flow rate.",
    "rationale": "A 645 µm × 177 µm × 35.1 mm rectangular channel is perfused with culture medium (μ = 0.001 Pa·s, ρ = 1060 kg/m³) at 14.02 µL/min. The wall shear stress is computed from the rectangular-channel relation τ = 6μQ/(w·h²), and the mean velocity from Q/A. The resulting shear (~0.069 Pa) sits in the low physiological range, appropriate for a low-shear sinusoidal/endothelial application. Reynolds number is well below 2300, confirming laminar flow.",
